# Drinking-water point service status -- TODO-1642, 2026-11-07
#
# The 16 drinking-water points were added after bldg1_synthetic_amenity_state.ttl was generated,
# so "is the water fountain on floor 2 working?" had no state to read. Re-running the generator
# would reshuffle every OTHER amenity's state (its draw is by position in a sorted list), so these
# records are separate, and each state is drawn from a hash of the point's own IRI: adding a point
# never moves another one. About 12% out of service, the generator's own rate.
#
# SERVICE STATE ONLY. Potability is never simulated (see the generator): a dispenser being out of
# order is a harmless demo; a simulated statement about whether water is safe to drink is not.

@prefix bldg: <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#> .
@prefix ontosage: <http://ontosage.org/capabilities#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

bldg:waterpoint_status_WaterPoint_Floor0_a a ontosage:AssetStatus ;
    ontosage:statusOf bldg:WaterPoint_Floor0_a ;
    ontosage:statusValue "operational" ;
    ontosage:statusSource "estates_helpdesk" ;
    ontosage:statusObservedAt "2026-11-07T04:46:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ontosage:assistanceContact "Estates helpdesk, ext 1234" .

